From 6e01462469eb0a34f2e874d0d73f07ba9f09d8db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyVerse <dev@pyverse.invalid>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 01:42:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Practice: solve a problem, then watch it execute

Adds the Practice -> Labs loop. After Run/Submit the problem page offers to
trace the learner's own code (or the reference solution) on one call, in the
same line-trace / memory-graph views Labs uses.

- tracer_runtime: trace_call() traces one call (`_result = fn(args)` appended and
  dimmed in the view); opt-in line-event limit raises TraceLimitExceeded
  (BaseException) so `while True:` ends instead of freezing the tab; `embedded`
  flag avoids a second PyScript tag. trace() with no args is unchanged (Labs).
- lab-engine.js: showTrace() split from runTrace(); window.PyverseLab hooks;
  harness lines dimmed; embedded Ctrl/Cmd+Enter. Labs page behaviour unchanged.
- problem page: Trace button, post-run prompt (accepted / failing visible case /
  crash), source toggle (yours / reference), `pyverse:trace` event for analytics.
  Hidden test inputs are never traced or shown.
- coding/trace_harness.py execs the shipped tracer in CPython (tests + QA).
- manage.py check_problem_traces: reference verifies, traces on first visible
  case, not cut off by the step cap. Fails CI on errors, --strict on warnings.
- 14 tests incl. a guard that the engine's element ids exist in the panel.
